eal when one backend serves the app. Requires session storage and sticky state if you scale horizontally."}, {"label": "JWTs", "description": "Signed stateless tokens the client sends with each request. No server-side session store, works well across multiple services/APIs or mobile clients. Harder to revoke before expiry — usually needs short-lived access tokens plus refresh-token rotation."}, {"label": "Hybrid (session cookie + JWT for APIs)", "description": "Sessions for the browser app, JWTs issued only where stateless access is needed (e.g., third-party API access or service-to-service calls). More moving parts, but each consumer gets the model that fits it."}], "multiSelect": false}], "answers": {"Which authentication approach do you prefer for this project?": "JWTs"}}, "tool_use_id": "toolu_01ArtigmS5jYufz6gsEbWCCb", "duration_ms": 0}, "held_ms": 7, "tool": "AskUserQuestion"}
